id: pm-915f
title: "Fail closed on exact all-source coverage, docstrings, lint, and duplication"
description: "The configured release gate now measures every src TypeScript file plus the new lifecycle but still accepts aggregate thresholds of 75 lines, 83 branches, and 64 functions. The current measurement is 77.01/87.31/67.74 rather than the required 100/100/100, other authored scripts remain excluded from the source set, and no repo-wide fail-closed docstring, strict lint, or duplication gate proves the user-required production-quality posture."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 0
tags[6]: coverage,docstrings,duplication,lint,quality-gate,release-blocker
created_at: "2026-08-07T19:46:07.962Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T19:59:15.305Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Behavior-driven tests cover every authored source and lifecycle path at exact 100/100/100; thresholds cannot be lowered or files silently omitted; docstring coverage is exact and quality-reviewed; strict erasable-TypeScript lint, no-any, no-dynamic-import, and duplication gates are mandatory in CI/release; npm and Bun gates plus real installed-CLI acceptance pass"
severity: critical
environment: pm-presets main at 853dd8e with Node 22 and installed pm 2026.8.7
repro_steps: "Run npm run coverage and inspect package.json coverageGate plus the release:check composition."
expected_result: "Every authored source and lifecycle path is enumerated by fail-closed gates and reaches exact 100/100/100 coverage with high-quality docstrings, strict lint, and zero unexplained duplication."
actual_result: "The current release gate passes at 77.01% lines, 87.31% branches, and 67.74% functions; the new lifecycle is included at exact 100/100/100, but other authored tooling and the broader source remain below exact coverage and docstring/lint/duplication gates are absent."
customer_impact: A green release gate currently cannot establish the requested full behavioral and documentation coverage.
body: ""
